---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

{/* Three sections, all of them about data.

       This page was renamed to /colophon and back again within the hour. The
       name "Colophon" is the tradition's word for this — the book page that
       credits everyone who made the object — and it fits: robinsloan.com has
       one, and of seven hand-picked independent blogs checked, it was the only
       one that had this page under either name. But it was the wrong word for a
       reader: of those seven, none would have known what it meant, and a link
       nobody clicks is not a page. Privacy is understood by everyone, it is the
       name the three sections below actually answer to, and "we collect nothing"
       is a privacy policy — an honest and unusually short one. Three of the four
       sections here are exactly that: no database, no cookies, no analytics, no
       third-party font request, and one sentence admitting the host keeps logs.

       The fourth was about authorship rather than data — the promise that
       nothing here was written by an AI system. That was always the odd one out
       on this page and it is on /about now, directly under the introduction. */}
<BaseLayout title="Privacy" lang="en">
    <article class="post-content">
        <h1>Privacy</h1>
        <p>This is a static file. No database, no backend, no log aggregation. No cookies, no analytics scripts, no user profiling, no A/B testing, no heatmaps, no ads.</p>
        <h2>Fonts</h2>
        <p>Text is set in Inter, served from this site's own domain as a single self-hosted font file. Because the font is served by us rather than a third party, loading it sends no request to anyone else.</p>
        <h2>Hosting</h2>
        <p>The site is served as static files from Cloudflare Pages. Like any web server, the host may retain request logs such as your IP address and the time of the request.</p>
    </article>
</BaseLayout>
